<div class="page-header">
  <h1>Settings</h1>
</div>

<div class="card form-card">
  <%= form_with url: settings_path, method: :patch do |f| %>
    <div class="field">
      <%= f.label :agent, "Agent" %>
      <%= f.select :agent, AiCli::Runner.available_agents, selected: @agent %>
      <p class="text-muted">The CLI used for all runs. Takes effect on the next run; runs already in progress keep their agent. Falls back to the AGENT env var until set here.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-actions">
      <%= f.submit "Save" %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>

<div class="card form-card">
  <h2>Workflow round robin</h2>
  <%= form_with url: settings_path, method: :patch do |f| %>
    <% @rotation.each do |name, weight| %>
      <div class="field">
        <%= label_tag "rotation_#{name}", name %>
        <%= number_field_tag "rotation[#{name}]", weight, min: 0, step: 1, id: "rotation_#{name}" %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
    <p class="text-muted">How many consecutive workflows each agent gets per cycle (e.g. claude 5, codex 3, cursor 1), to spread usage limits. Each workflow keeps its agent for its whole life; a stage's own agent still wins. All zeros turns it off and the agent above is used. The agent above (and brainstorm, syncs) is still used for non-workflow tasks.</p>

    <div class="form-actions">
      <%= f.submit "Save round robin" %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
